		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5153&amp;p=37302#p37302"><![CDATA[
anyone else seeing this?<br><br>md-uv390, 20240908fw, analog fm, vfo or memory, press #, "DTMF ENTRY" on screen, i type allstar command "*312345", hit the green button, radio keys up, dtmf sequence is transmitted and received fine.  works for any sequence.<br><br>problem is the squelch stays closed after the radio stops transmitting and i don't hear the reply from the node.<br><br>i mean, after the transmit, red led turns off, then led turns green as the node responds, but the squelch does not open.  if i hit the red button, then the squelch opens.  seeing this on both tyt and stm cpu uv390.<br><br>i just tried that if i do into menu&gt;contacts&gt;fm-dtmf-contacts and transmit one of the string memories, same thing happens, squelch stays closed, i have to hit the red button many times and back all the way out of the menu before squelch will open.  <br><br>pretty sure this used to work ok.  i just upgraded the fw to 20240908 on on 3x uv390 and they all do the same.  i know there is a newer beta version, but has this been fixed in that version? i was going to wait till the beta went release.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=403">AF6MQ</a> — Sat May 31, 2025 12:56 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
